// Weapons MomentumPorter can port into Momentum's weapon slots, per source game.
// Paths are game paths in the source game. "sounds" maps a sound role (the keys of Momentum's
// scripts/server_weapon/weapon_momentum_<slot>.txt SoundData: single_shot, explosion, trail, fizzle, fizzle_alt,
// deploy, swish, stab, hit, hit_wall, zoom, bounce, charge, ...) to a soundscript entry of the source game ("" silences
// it). Games Momentum doesn't mount use "waves" (game paths under sound/) instead. "slots" lists the Momentum
// weapons it fits, best first. A game's "loadout" picks the weapon that building all of its weapons puts in a Momentum
// weapon several fit best (else the first listed), or adds one to a weapon it fits but not best. See WeaponCatalog.cs
// for every field.
